WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:04.510
What exactly are you suggesting?

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:06.370
(SINGING) Mr.
Bright, Mr. Bright,

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:07.750
you are in for such a treat.

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:09.430
I have got some little dolls--

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:14.920
darling sprouts-- here abouts
that I'd love for you to meet.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:15.790
Step right up.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.590
Sir, welcome to the
Bright's butcher shop.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:20.980
What can we get for you today?

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.470
Have you any ham?

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:25.690
Ah! (SINGING) Courtesy of Sam.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.520
How about veal?

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.730
Yes, (SINGING)
thanks to Camille.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.510
Kidney?

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:32.650
(SINGING) Sydney.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:33.610
Belly?

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:34.450
(SINGING) Kelly.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:35.110
Lamb?

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:39.010
(SINGING) That's Pam with
some jam or mint jelly.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.700
I'd love some ground beef.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.790
(SINGING) Well then,
sir, you're in luck.

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:44.180
Which do you prefer?

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:47.022
We've got Patty or Chuck.

00:00:47.022 --> 00:00:50.640
[LAUGHTER]

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.100
Have you any mutton?

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.570
That would be Sutton.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.380
Perhaps some foie gras?

00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:00.600
(SINGING) Voile, see Francois.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.620
Baloney?

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:02.370
(SINGING) Tony.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.420
Salami?

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:04.140
(SINGING) Tommy.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.920
And we've also got Reuben
if you like pastrami.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.910
But do you have mincemeat?

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:11.580
(SINGING) Well,
since meat is sparse,

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.210
we've got Vince meat instead
sliced right off of his--

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:18.300
Caldwell, please, there
are children present.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.590
Not for long.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:23.412
No, because we're going to kill
them and sell them as meat.

00:01:23.412 --> 00:01:26.184
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:26.184 --> 00:01:27.570
Hey.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.320
(SINGING) Ain't got no dad.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.930
Ain't got no mom.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:38.480
But are they sad
or are they glum?

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.250
(SINGING) No, they come
from a world that's

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:44.930
boiling with the sweetest
smiles you've ever seen.

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:49.130
Oh, they're good enough to eat.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:51.620
Delicious!

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:53.000
(SINGING) A job well done--

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.320
(SINGING) A job well done--

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.710
--is, oh, so rare.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:56.900
--is, oh, so rare.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.340
When Santa sung--

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.570
When Santa sung--

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:01.220
--the cupboard's bare.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.600
So bare.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:05.750
Before these darlings
get much thinner,

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:08.990
I think we ought to
make them dinner.

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:12.314
Oh, they're good enough to eat.

00:02:12.314 --> 00:02:13.147
Supper time!

00:02:13.147 --> 00:02:13.730
[BELL RINGING]

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:14.680
Careful!

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:17.000
Oh, I could take an eye out!

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.520
(SINGING) We may
not be respectable,

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.250
but we are so delectable.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:25.670
Don't mean to be
presumptuous, but truth

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.880
is we are scrumptious.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:32.680
Cakes and candies--
they're half as sweet.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:37.126
Ooh, we're good enough to eat.

00:02:37.126 --> 00:02:39.640
[WHISTLE]

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.040
(SINGING) Ain't got no dad.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.240
We may not be respectable.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.710
Ain't got no mom.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:44.930
But we are so delectable.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.424
But are they sad?

00:02:46.424 --> 00:02:47.918
Don't mean to be presumptuous--

00:02:47.918 --> 00:02:48.914
Or are they glum?

00:02:48.914 --> 00:02:50.906
--but truth is we
are scrumptious.

00:02:50.906 --> 00:02:52.570
No, they come from
a world that's

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:56.630
boiling with the sweetest
smells you've ever seen.

00:02:56.630 --> 00:03:00.318
Ooh, they're good enough to eat.

00:03:00.318 --> 00:03:03.306
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:15.258
[TAPPING]

00:03:18.246 --> 00:03:23.740
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.915
(DRAWN-OUT SINGING)

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.285
(SINGING) When times is hard--

00:03:34.285 --> 00:03:35.470
When times is hard--

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:36.520
--you must make do.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:37.870
--you must make do.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.684
Pull out of a blonde.

00:03:39.684 --> 00:03:40.940
Pull out a blonde.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:41.816
Try Mary Lou.

00:03:41.816 --> 00:03:43.570
And try her brother too.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:46.480
Yes, when you lack
a key ingredient,

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:49.510
substitutes become expedient.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:52.020
Ooh, they're good enough--

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.110
though they're kind of tough--

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:59.810
ooh, they're good enough to eat.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:01.910
Good to eat!

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.310
Good to eat!

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.710
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:08.860
Eat-- good to eat!

